        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "tenacity  he  had  fought  his  way  to  the  front,  and \nthe  son  of  the  obscure  renegade  of  Mitylene  died \na  king.  It  is  true  that  his  sovereignty  was  pre- \ncarious, that  it  was  maintained  at  the  edge  of  the \nsword  ;  none  the  less,  in  that  welter  of  anarchy \nin  which  he  lived  he  had  forced  himself  to  the  sum- \nmit, and,  pirate,  sea-wolf,  and  robber  as  he  was, \nwe  cannot  withhold  from  him  a  meed  of  the  most \nhearty  admiration.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
