      {
        "finding_id": "section-15b13469e9e7b2b11ee1",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "That  warrior,  nothing  disconcerted,  pursued  his \nway  to  the  island  of  Zante,  where  he  fell  in  with \na  Turkish  \"  not  a,\"  under  the  command  of  the \nBashas  Zay  and  Himeral.  To  these  officers  of  the \nGrand  Turk  Barbarossa  used  most  injurious  lan- \nguage, bitterly  reproaching  them  with  not  having \nsought  out  and  destroyed  Andrea  Doria,  which  he \ndeclared  they  ought  to  and  should  have  done. \nThis  is  yet  another  instance  of  the  extraordinary \ncharacter  of  the  man.  These  persons  were  the \nhighest  officers  in  the  fleet  of  the  Ottoman  Empire ; \nit  was  more  than  possible  that  they  would  be  placed \nunder  the  command  of  Barbarossa  as  soon  as  his \nnew  position  as  Admiralissimo  was  adjusted  at  Con- \nstantinople ;  and  yet,  in  spite  of  these  facts,  the \ncorsair  had  taken  the  very  first  opportunity  which \npresented  itself  grossly  to  insult  these  men.  It  is \ntrue,  as  we  shall  see,  that  his  injurious  words  came \nhome  to  roost  in  the  future  ;  but  arrogant,  conquer- \ning, contemptuous,  Barbarossa  seems  to  have \nshouldered  his  way  through  life,  fearing  none  and \nfeared  by  all.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
