        "evidence_excerpt": "All  this  harmonised  well  with  his  reputation  as  a \nchief  so  resolute,  so  pitiless,  that  it  was  the  boast \nof  his  followers  that  his  very  name  shouted  in \nbattle  put  to  flight  the  Christian  vessels.  His  smile \nwas  fine  and  malicious,  his  speech  facile,  revealing \nbeneath  the  rude  exterior  of  the  corsair  the  subtle \nman  of  affairs,  who,  from  nothing,  had  made  himself \nKing  of  Algiers,  and  was  now,  by  the  invitation  of \nSoliman  the  Magnificent,  Admiralissimo  of  the  Otto- \nman navy.",
