        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "as  we  have  seen,  even  advocates  that  a  certain \nminimum  of  consideration  should  be  shown  to  them \nin  order  that  better  work  might  be  obtained.  It \nwas  probable,  however,  that  in  the  case  of  the \nChristian  slaves  captured  by  the  corsairs  even  this \nminimum  was  to  seek,  as  the  numbers  swept  off \nby  them  were  so  enormous  that  they  could  be  used \nup  and  replaced  without  inconveniencing  these \nrovers  of  the  sea,  to  whom  compassion  for  suffering \nwas  absolutely  unknown.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
