      {
        "finding_id": "section-d71c6a71c3fd5ffda481",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "IN  character,  in  capability,  in  strategic  insight, \nin  tactical  ability,  not  one  of  the  predecessors \nor  the  successors  of  Kheyr-ed-Din  Barbarossa  can \nbe  compared  to  him  ;  he  was  the  greatest  and  most \noutstanding  figure  of  all  those  corsairs  of  whose \ndeeds  we  hear  so  much  during  the  sixteenth  cen- \ntury, the  man  above  all  others  who  was  feared  and \nhated  by  his  contemporaries  in  Christendom.  He \nlived,  as  we  have  said,  for  another  eight  years  after \nthe  battle  of  Prevesa,  but  his  great  age  prevented  him \nfrom  pursuing  a  very  active  career.  There  were, \nhowever,  other  and  younger  men,  trained  in  the \nterrible  school  of  hardship  in  which  his  life  had  been \npassed,  who  proved  themselves  to  be  his  very  worthy \nsuccessors,  even  if  they  did  not  display  the  same \ngenius  hi  war  and  statecraft.  The  conditions  of \nthis  period  are  somewhat  remarkable  when  we \ncome  to  consider  them ;  Europe,  which  had  been \nsunk  in  a  rude  and  uncultured  barbarism  during \nthe  middle  ages,  was  emerging  under  the  influence \nof  the  Renaissance  into  a  somewhat  higher  and \nnobler  conception  of  life.  It  is  true  that  the  awak-",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
