        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Once  again  had  a  Moslem  corsair  bid  defiance \nto  that  ruler  whom  Sandoval  and  Marmol  in  their \nhistories  greet  by  the  name  of  the  \"  Modern  Cassar.\" \nIt  was  told  to  Charles  that  Susa,  Sf ax,  and  Monastir \nhad  fallen,  that  \"  Africa  \"  was  in  the  hands  of  the \ncorsairs;  \"was  he  never  to  be  free/ from  these \npestilent  knaves,\"  he  demanded  of  his  trembling \ncourtiers  ?  Hot-foot  came  the  couriers  from \nCharles  to  Andrea  Dona,  with  orders  to  take  Dragut \ndead  or  alive,  but  alive  for  choice  ;  and  up  and",
