          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "any  influence  on  the  Sultan  it  is  impossible  to  say ; \nhe  was  in  the  habit  of  employing  the  corsairs,  and \napparently  cared  nothing  about  their  piratical \nreputation,  so  long  as  their  depredations  were  con- \nfined to  Christian  vessels.  Shortly  after  the  re- \nceipt of  the  answer  of  Charles,  however,  the  Sultan \nconferred  upon  Dragut  the  title  of  Sandjak  or \ngovernor  of  the  island  of  Santa  Maura,  thus  con- \nstituting him  a  Turkish  official.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
