      {
        "finding_id": "section-8c344938b1d5496cc28f",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "On  June  i6th  another  attack  was  made  on  the  for- \ntress, and,  incredible  as  it  may  seem,  it  was  repulsed \nwith  such  awful  slaughter  that  at  last  the  Turks \nwould  not  face  the  swords  of  the  garrison.  After \nthis  the  enemy  succeeded  in  drawing  so  close  a \ncordon  round  the  place  that  no  more  succours  could \nreach  it,  and  the  end  was  but  a  matter  of  time.  The \nday  before  it  came  Dragut,  who,  with  his  usual \nintrepidity,  was  standing  in  the  midst  of  a  hot  fire, \nwas  struck  on  the  side  of  the  head  by  a  stone  dis- \nlodged from  a  wall  by  a  cannon-ball.  At  the  moment \nwhen  this  happened  he  was  holding  a  council  of  war \nin  the  trenches  with  Piali,  a  Sanjak,  and  the  principal \nTurkish  engineer.  The  same  shot  which  wounded \nDragut  killed  the  Sanjak  on  the  spot.  Piali  caused \na  cloak  to  be  thrown  over  the  body  of  the  corsair  in \norder  that  his  state  should  not  be  observed  by  the \nsoldiers,  and  as  soon  as  possible  had  him  removed \nto  his  tent,  where  he  lay  unconscious  till  the  follow- \ning day.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
