          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The third is the French justificatory account written after 1830, which needed a nest \nof pirates and a decayed tyranny to justify the conquest. Much of the administrative \ndetail in circulation comes from it, including the editions through which the Regency's \nown documents survive, and the study uses those editions for the documents while \ndeclining the frame.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
