        "verified": false
      },
      {
        "finding_id": "section-4174880117fbba70dbb8",
        "file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The Regency Of Algiers",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic",
          "date": [
            "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The study began from a seed written at the close of the previous build, and from a \npage, written before any research, recording what training had left about the Regency: \na pirate state; deys mostly murdered; corsairing arriving with the Turks and dying after \n1816; a decayed despotism falling in three weeks. The seed was scaffolding, not a cage. \nWhere the evidence disagreed with it, or with that page, the evidence won, and the \ncorrections are recorded here rather than argued in the modules.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
          "source_file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 10143,
          "end_char": 10642,
          "start_line": 271,
          "end_line": 276,
          "printed_page": null,
          "scan_indexes_0_based": [],
          "pdf_file": null,
          "original_inspected": false
        },
        "reported_cited_pages": [],
        "decision": "REVIEW_CONTEXT",
        "reason": "THEMATIC_SOURCE_PASSAGE_NOT_VERIFIED_BASE",
        "extraction_method": "DETERMINISTIC_THEMATIC_PASSAGE_READING",
        "uncertainties": [
          "ORIGINAL_NOT_INSPECTED",
          "SOURCE_GENEALOGY_PENDING",
          "INDEPENDENCE_UNRESOLVED",
          "TOPONYM_AND_USAGE_REQUIRE_SEMANTIC_EXTRACTION",
          "DATE_OUTSIDE_SCOPE",
          "REGIONAL_SCOPE_REQUIRES_REVIEW"
        ],
        "evidence_state": "ACQUIRED",
        "original_inspected": false,
        "verified": false
      },
      {
        "finding_id": "section-ac04b8823b91f04adb8e",
        "file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The Regency Of Algiers",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic",
          "date": [
            "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The starting page expected corsairing to be the order's main revenue and to have \narrived with the Turks. Leo Africanus records that the townsmen of Algiers had built \ngalleys and raided the Balearics before the brothers came, which is why Ferdinand built \nhis fort. In the one year whose accounts survive, 1822, prizes contributed nothing; \ntribute, monopolies, the estates of the dead and the rents of confiscated property \nsupplied more than the provinces. The prize register shows corsairing large and volatile \nin the war years, not constant. And the order did not fall because it could not pay: the \nFrench found nearly forty-nine million francs in the Kasba. It fell to a fracture at its \napex in 1817, the loss of its income from the sea in 1816, and a conquest in 1830.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
          "source_file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 13047,
          "end_char": 13825,
          "start_line": 321,
          "end_line": 329,
          "printed_page": null,
          "scan_indexes_0_based": [],
          "pdf_file": null,
          "original_inspected": false
        },
        "reported_cited_pages": [],
        "decision": "REVIEW_CONTEXT",
        "reason": "THEMATIC_SOURCE_PASSAGE_NOT_VERIFIED_BASE",
        "extraction_method": "DETERMINISTIC_THEMATIC_PASSAGE_READING",
        "uncertainties": [
          "ORIGINAL_NOT_INSPECTED",
          "SOURCE_GENEALOGY_PENDING",
