        "evidence_excerpt": "Landscape — the ground on the eve. A Simple Stranger. The central Maghrib \nbetween the Spanish landings of 1509 and the sultans firman of 1519: a coast on which \nevery town, tribe and dynasty was already paying someone for protection, where \ncorsairing was older than the Turks, and where two captains from Lesbos were hired by \nthe town of Algiers against a Spanish fort, killed their employer in his bath, and \nborrowed from Istanbul the sermon and the coin they could not mint.",
