        "evidence_excerpt": "The study's principal public-domain debts are these. Leo Africanus, in John Pory's \nEnglish translation of 1600, as reprinted by the Hakluyt Society in 1896. The \nTopographia, e historia general de Argel (1612), printed under the name of Diego de \nHaedo. Fondation de la Régence d'Alger: histoire des Barberousse, the brothers’ \nchronicle, translated by Sander Rang and Ferdinand Denis (1837). Pierre Dan, Histoire \nde Barbarie et de ses corsatres (1649). A Compleat History of the Piratical States of \nBarbary (1750), Joseph Morgan's English version of Laugier de Tassy. The Revue \nafricaine, especially vol. 4 (1860) for the covenant of 1749, vol. 12 (1868) for the \nzawiya deed, vols 15-16 (1871-72) for the prize register, vols 40-41 (1896-97) for \nVenture de Paradis and the description of the kingdom under the last dey. Albert \nDevoulx, Epigraphie indigene du Musée archéologique d'Alger (1874). William Shaler, \nSketches of Algiers (1826). Eugene Plantet, Correspondance des deys d'Alger avec la cour",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1600,
          1612,
          1649
        ],
