      {
        "finding_id": "section-4ad11a108a92ce9fc8ea",
        "file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The Regency Of Algiers",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic",
          "date": [
            "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Three things should be fixed from this before the brothers enter, because each \nshapes what they were able to do. The first is that the town's revenue, in the decade \nbefore the conquest, was flowing outward — to Bougie, to a tribal prince, to Spain — \nand in each case it purchased a protection that stopped at the edge of the protector's \nreach. The second is that Algiers already had galleys and already used them: Leo says \nplainly that the townsmen had built ships and raided the Balearic islands, and that this \nwas the reason Ferdinand sent his armada and built his fort. Corsairing on this coast \ndid not arrive with the Turks; the Spanish fort was a response to it, and the fort's two \nhundred men were a tax collected on the town's own seafaring. The third is the most \nimportant and the easiest to miss. Haedo's sentence ends not with a Spanish reverse or \na rising of the town but with a death. The truce was a contract with a man, and when \nthe man died in January 1516 the townsmen treated the obligation as having died with \nhim. Nothing on this shore — not the tribute to Bougie, not the protection of the \nMitidja prince, not the ten-year truce with Spain — outlived the reach or the life of the",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
          "source_file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 31286,
          "end_char": 32498,
          "start_line": 673,
          "end_line": 686,
          "printed_page": null,
          "scan_indexes_0_based": [],
