        "evidence_excerpt": "coast on which every town, dynasty and tribe was already paying someone for \nprotection, on which corsairing was older than the Turks and was the reason for the \nSpanish fort, and on which no arrangement — not tribute to Bougie, not a tribal \nprince's protection, not a ten-year truce with Ferdinand — survived the death or the \nretreat of the party it was made with. The brothers did not bring instability to that",
