      {
        "finding_id": "section-29b361cd62d9f13466f4",
        "file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The Regency Of Algiers",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic",
          "date": [
            "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The corsair captains commanded crews paid in shares of prizes, and the captains, \nmany of them renegades from Christian Europe, formed a corporation of their own. \nHaedo says that for many years no corsair or renegade who was not a Turk by nation \ncould be a janissary, and that the corsairs in turn refused to let janissaries sail with them, \nbecause the janissaries wanted the profits of the sea and the corsairs wanted to keep \nthem. The quarrel was settled, he records, by Mehmed Pasha, son of Salah Rais, \"Rey \nde Argel,” \"reconciliando a los genizaros con los cosarios, porque sobre esto auia entre \nellos muy grande enemistad,” reconciling the janissaries with the corsairs, because there \nwas very great enmity between them over this, and it was ordered \"que los genizaros \npudiessen yr en los nauios de corso por soldados, y que todo cosario, o renegado \nquando quisiesse pudiesse entrar en el numero” — that janissaries might go aboard the \ncorsair ships as soldiers, and that any corsair or renegade who wished might enter the \nnumber, and draw the pay, of the janissaries. The two corporations were joined by \nadmitting each into the other's income. The janissary acquired a share of the sea; the \ncorsair acquired a place on the pay register and the rank that came with it.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
