      {
        "finding_id": "section-2bb08bff4067e648c606",
        "file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The Regency Of Algiers",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic",
          "date": [
            "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Quoted exactly, and how verified. Haedo, Topographia, e historia general de Argel \n(1612; archiveorg topographiaehistOOha): the passages on Khayr al-Din's \nrequest to the sultan, the reconciliation of janissaries and corsairs, the sons and \ngrandsons of janissaries, the corps's strength of up to six thousand and three thousand \nfive hundred to four thousand at Algiers, the column as \"rico corso,” the recruit's four \ndoblas, the retiring agha's twenty-five doblas and the three and four aghas a year, and \nthe taking of the islet and death of Vargas, were each read directly from images of the \nprinted page; long s is printed as s and the renderings are mine. The Laugier account is \nquoted from A Compleat History of the Piratical States of Barbary (London, 1750; \narchiveorg bim_eighteenth-century_a-compleat-history-of- \nth_gentleman-who-resided-th_1750), Joseph Morgan's English version \nof Laugier de Tassy's Histoire du royaume d'Alger (1725) with additions; the passages \non the Porte's recruits and money, the twelve thousand \"Turks in Pay,\" the recruiting \nrule, the first and closed pay, and the state officers’ closed pay were confirmed by \nindependent OCR of cropped lines, and one text-layer error (\"In N of Men\") was \ncorrected from the page to \"In a Scarcity of Men.\" The ahd al-aman of 1749 is quoted \nfrom its French version by A. Devoulkx fils in Revue africaine 4 (1860), from p. 211 \n(archive.org f r301af riqueO4); the numbers in the attendance clause and the pay- \nreward clause were confirmed by independent OCR (the attendance clause is given in \nparaphrase because the print of its rank names is damaged), and the kasba and \"sous les \nordres du divan\" passages were read from the page image.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1612
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
