        "evidence_excerpt": "The last is what I expected and did not find. I expected the Regency's claims to \nEurope and its claims to the faithful to be flatly inconsistent — a holy war that signed \ntreaties. The warrant document itself joins them. The investiture that calls the \nAlgerines the champions of the faith also forbids them to harm the powers holding the \nPorte's safe-conduct, and the law of war that made a captured Christian lawful spoil \nalso made a treaty a grant of protection. The inconsistency was in the eye of the \nEuropean reader, who saw piracy and diplomacy where the Regency saw war and",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
