        "evidence_excerpt": "And last, what I expected and did not find. I expected an order that held its \npopulation by terror, because that is what the word pirate state implies. What the \nwitnesses describe is a single city in which both ends of the scale were running at once: \na townsman whose compliance was nearly free and richly rewarded, living in the same \nstreets as a captive whose compliance bought nothing but survival and whose refusal \nwould be answered by the worst the order could inflict. The terror was real, and it was",
        "years_in_scope": [],
