        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The deficit was paid from the hoard in the Kasba. Shaler says that the fruits of the \ncorsairs had not only supplied all the order's wants until recent years but had allowed a \ntreasury of gold and silver to be hoarded that might sustain it for many years to come. \nIn 1822, then, the order was living on its capital, drawing down gold and silver \naccumulated in the decades when the prize register's totals ran into millions of francs.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
