        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Following the money one stage further shows where the extraction finally went. The \n$700,000 paid to the soldiers was spent in the city, and much of it on what the city \nimported. Shaler's trade table for the same year records imports of $1,200,000 — \nBritish and Indian manufactures, silks and brocades from Leghorn, sugar, coffee and \npepper from France, raw silk from the Levant, and jewels, diamonds and silver plate \nfrom France and Italy worth $100,000 — against exports of $273,000. \"The balance of \nnine hundred and twenty-seven thousand dollars, enormous for a country of so few \nactive resources as Algiers, is remitted annually in gold and silver.\" The tribute of \nChristian kings, the monopoly on the tribesman’s hides, the estates of the heirless and \nthe hoard of the corsair years ended their journey as coin shipped to Marseilles,",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
