        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Contested figures and what is not counted. The 1822 table comes from an \nunnamed informant and describes one year; it cannot be extended backward to the \ncorsair years. The percentage shares are arithmetic on that table alone. The prize series \nhas gaps, including 1781-92 and several single years, and records gross proceeds before \ndivision, excluding hulls. No total of extraction is given, because the grain in kind, the \nprovincial retentions, the monopoly producers’ loss, the salt monopoly's yield and the \nvalue of forced labour are not quantified in any source reached. Weak links. No source \nreached records currency or mint profits, so that mechanism is not assessed; tax on the \ntribes is known only as the provincial remittance, not as the rates the tribes paid; and \nthe rural labour obligations of subject tribes on state lands, described in French \nliterature after 1830, were not reached. Drops. The sums the United States paid under \nits treaty of 1795, recorded in the American naval documents, were not used because",
