        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The fourth is that the Regency’s image abroad was made by its own class of \nintermediaries on the other side of the sea, with interests of their own. The friars who \nransomed captives needed charity and were accused by a consular writer of spreading \nfalsehood to get it; the consular writer wanted the Algerines understood and saw his \nbook sold in England as a history of pirates.",
