      {
        "finding_id": "section-9e87712d9dceee55b9fb",
        "file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The Regency Of Algiers",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic",
          "date": [
            "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The witnesses reached in this study establish the end of thirteen of the thirty. Nine \nof those thirteen were killed by their own order or removed by force, and in each case \nthe witness says so plainly. Devoulx, commenting on the Regency's inscriptions in \n1874, records that the dey \"El-Hadj Chaban, élu en 1100 et étranglé en 1106\" — \nelected in 1689 and strangled in 1695. The Laugier account records \"Hali Dey, who \nobtained the Deylik by the Murder of Ibrahim Dey, sirnamed the Madman, in June \n1710.\" Devoulx records that Abdi was elected in 1724 \"4 la suite de I'assassinat de \nMehammed pacha\"; that Mohammed, the dey called el-Retorto, \"fut assassiné le 11 \ndécembre 1754, au moment ot il présidait la solde des janissaires\" — was assassinated at \nthe moment he was presiding over the payment of the janissaries; that \"Mustapha \npacha fut assassiné par la milice le 30 aot\" 1805; that his successor's successor, Ali \nKhodja, was \"étranglé par ordre de la milice\" in 1809; and that Hajji Ali was strangled in \nhis bath in March 1815. Shaler records that Omar, surprised in his palace by \nconspirators in September 1817, \"was strangled on the spot.\" And the last dey, Hussein, \nwas removed in 1830 by the French.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1689,
          1695
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
          "source_file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
