        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Contested figures. The tally of ends is given as \"at least” figures over the nineteen \nestablished cases, with eleven unestablished, and no percentage of the thirty is offered. \nPlantet's list and the modern accounts differ on some late-seventeenth-century names \nand dates, and Plantet’s is followed. Weak links. The periodisation into two violent \nbands and a quiet middle rests partly on the modern accounts for the late eighteenth \ncentury; the eleven unknown ends cluster in the violent periods and would, if \nestablished, most likely strengthen the violent share there rather than alter the middle. \nNo source reached records the corsair captains’ or the kouloughlis' conduct after 1816 \nor describes the beys' calculations in their own words. Drops. A frequently repeated \nstatement that a stated majority of deys were murdered was not used, because no source",
        "years_in_scope": [],
