      {
        "finding_id": "section-9537aaafc60951d8f9f1",
        "file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The Regency Of Algiers",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic",
          "date": [
            "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "His successor did. Ali Khodja, Shaler writes, learning of conspiracies against him, \n\"transferred his residence, together with the public treasury,” from the ancient palace of \nthe deys \"into the citadel, where he organized a guard of natives for his protection, and \nset the Turks at defiance.” Rumour in the city put the treasury carried up on mules at \nfifty million dollars. \"This chief appears to have formed the project of suppressing \nentirely the corps of Janissaries, and probably that of rendering the sovereignty \nhereditary in his family,\" and he persecuted the Turks with violence throughout his \nshort reign. He died of the plague in 1818, and his successor, Hussein, \"continues to \nprefer the secure residence of the citadel.\"",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
          "source_file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 277958,
          "end_char": 278699,
          "start_line": 5232,
          "end_line": 5240,
          "printed_page": null,
          "scan_indexes_0_based": [],
          "pdf_file": null,
          "original_inspected": false
        },
