        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Quoted exactly, and how verified. The covenant of 1749, in Devoulx fils's French \nversion (Revue africaine 4, 1860, pp. 211 ff; archive.org fr30laf riqueQ4): the \namnesty, the clause on the hair split in forty, the clause on examination before \njudgment, the declaration that the janissaries' children shall be janissaries, the \nprohibition of news-letters on pain of beheading, and the written resolutions, were \nread from images of the printed page or confirmed by independent OCR of cropped \nlines. Haedo (1612): the admission of corsairs and renegades to the number of the \njanissaries, read from the page image earlier in this study. Shaler, Sketches of Algiers \n(1826): Ali Khodja's transfer of residence and treasury into the citadel and his \"guard of \nnatives,\" his project of suppressing the janissaries and rendering the sovereignty \nhereditary, Hussein's preference for the citadel, the right of asylum \"never ... \nrecognised,” the strangers \"protected in their rights here,” the consul's inviolability, and \nconvicts \"in lieu of slaves,” were confirmed by independent OCR or read from the page \nimage. Dan (1649): \"CHARALA, CHARALA, c'est a dire iustice de Dieu,” read from \nthe page image earlier in this study. Shaler's \"probably through corruption\" and \n\"aberrations\" were verified earlier.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1612,
          1649
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
