      {
        "finding_id": "section-aa315f646583dcf5a5a5",
        "file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The Regency Of Algiers",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic",
          "date": [
            "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "6138c424ee238e85fb6fb48ba525f1c29c7f976cf104138f88baec22a14297cd",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The standing number of captives is given twice by Pierre Dan, a redemptionist, \nfrom his time in Algiers in the 1630s, and the two figures measure different things. \nAcross the corsair cities of Barbary, he writes, \"Le nombre de ces pauures captifs se \nmonte 4 peu prés a trente-six mille, selon le dénombrement que j’en ay pt auoir sur les \nlieux, & les memoires qui m'en ont esté fournis & enuoyez par les Consuls Chrestiens\" \n— the number of these poor captives amounts to about thirty-six thousand, according \nto the count he could make on the spot and the memoranda the Christian consuls sent \nhim. For the kingdom of Algiers alone, he says he was told by several Christians, Turks \nand renegades well versed in the country's affairs that in the city, the villages and the \nplaces within twenty-five leagues \"il y auoit prés de vingt-cing mille Chrestiens captifs : \nEt parmy ceux-cy, quinze cens Francois, auec plus de deux cens femmes” — there were \nnearly twenty-five thousand Christian captives, among them fifteen hundred French, \nwith more than two hundred women. Dan's order raised money by the number of \ncaptives it could show, and his figures should be read with that in mind; they are \nnonetheless a count and an informed estimate, and they are the best standing figures \nreached for the seventeenth century.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1630
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/the-regency-of-algiers",
          "source_file": "the-regency-of-algiers_The_Regency_of_Algiers_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 310203,
          "end_char": 311527,
